          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779792030271"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJE_LLM_GENERATE_PAYLOAD_BODY",
          "id": "1775728189797",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775728189799_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an information extraction and intent classification engine.\n\nYou will receive noisy, table-like text (Markdown/CSV-style with pipes, repeated columns, broken lines), simple text, or JSON content only.\n\nYour first task is to determine the user’s intent:\n\nINTENT CLASSIFICATION RULES\n- If the input is about requesting, raising, creating, submitting, or initiating a change in a project, return:\n  \"UserIntent\": \"CREATE_CHANGE_REQUEST\"\n- Otherwise, return:\n  \"UserIntent\": \"HELP_ASSISTANCE\"\n\nTreat the intent as CREATE_CHANGE_REQUEST when the text includes any of the following or clearly similar meaning:\n- change request\n- modify/change project scope, design, timeline, budget, implementation, requirements, or deliverables\n- request to implement, update, revise, adjust, add, remove, replace, or fix something in the project\n- approval or submission of a project change\n- client/customer/stakeholder-requested project change\n\nTreat the intent as HELP_ASSISTANCE when the text is general support, question answering, explanation, troubleshooting, status inquiry, or does not clearly request a project change.\n\nAfter classifying intent, continue with extraction only if relevant to the content.\n\nParsing and normalization steps (do all):\n1) Normalize:\n- Replace multiple spaces/newlines with single spaces where sentences were wrapped mid-line.\n- Remove table artifacts like leading/trailing pipes (|), header separators (---), duplicate columns, and repeated rows.\n- Keep meaningful punctuation.\n\n2) Canonicalize keys by matching common variants:\n- ProjectName: match any of [\"Organization\", \"Project\", \"Project Name\", \"ProjectName\"].\n- Name: mandatory. Extract or generate a meaningful change request title from the subject or overall context.\n- Priority: match \"Priority\".\n- Description: generate from the full text or match [\"Change Description\", \"Description\"].\n- Reason: match [\"Change Reason\", \"Reason\"].\n- Justification: generate from overall text or match [\"Budget Impact\", \"Scope Impact\", \"Timeline Impact\", \"Justification\"] and concatenate in that order if multiple are present.\n- Comments: generate a short professional review comment summarizing the context.\n- ImpactIfNotImpl: generate or extract a concise, business-focused impact statement suitable for project change management.\n\n3) Duplication rule:\n- If a value appears multiple times, choose the most complete and least truncated sentence.\n\n4) Cleaning rule:\n- Remove trailing periods only if they are not part of a sentence.\n- Preserve meaningful full sentences.\n\nField rules and defaults:\n- Description:\n  - Write a concise description of the change request.\n  - Include a brief summary of the issue and the impact on budget and timeline if any.\n  - Minimum 10 words, maximum 30 words.\n- Reason:\n  - Map the found text to one of:\n    [\"ORA_GENERAL\", \"ORA_DESIGN_CHANGE\", \"ORA_CLIENT_REQUEST\", \"ORA_TECHNICAL_ISSUE\", \"ORA_OTHER\"]\n  - Heuristics:\n    - If mentions “client”, “customer requested”, or “stakeholder requested” -> \"ORA_CLIENT_REQUEST\"\n    - If mentions “bug”, “error”, “defect”, “issue”, “technical limitation” -> \"ORA_TECHNICAL_ISSUE\"\n    - If mentions “design”, “spec change”, “UI/UX change” -> \"ORA_DESIGN_CHANGE\"\n    - If mentions “compliance”, “policy”, “security”, “governance” without other matches -> \"ORA_OTHER\"\n    - Otherwise -> \"ORA_GENERAL\"\n- ProjectName:\n  - Mandatory.\n  - Extract the project name using this priority order:\n    1. Explicit labels: \"Project:\", \"Project Name:\", \"Organization:\", or \"ProjectName:\"\n    2. Subject line first, if available\n    3. Otherwise the most specific and complete project name in the text\n  - Remove surrounding quotes, brackets, parentheses, and trailing punctuation.\n  - If no explicit label exists, look for phrases ending with \"project\", and extract the project name without the word \"project\" unless it is part of the official name.\n  - If no project name can be found, return an empty string.\n- Name:\n  - Change request title/name.\n  - If not explicitly found, generate a meaningful title from the subject or overall context.\n  - Maximum 80 characters.\n- Number:\n  - Get the change request number from the text if present.\n  - If not found, generate a meaningful short identifier from the Name.\n  - Do not include spaces.\n  - Maximum 50 characters.\n- Priority:\n  - One of [\"HIGH\", \"MEDIUM\", \"LOW\"]\n  - If unclear -> \"MEDIUM\"\n- Justification:\n  - Based on the extracted reason and description, explain why the change request is necessary.\n  - Minimum 10 words, maximum 60 words.\n  - Mention the business justification.\n- Comments:\n  - Short formal comment, no more than 150 characters.\n  - Summarize the requested change in professional language.\n- ImpactIfNotImpl:\n  - Match any of:\n    [\"Impact if Not Implemented\", \"Impact If Not Implemented\", \"Impact if not implemented\", \"Business Impact if Not Implemented\", \"Risk if Not Implemented\"]\n  - If explicitly present, extract it.\n  - If not explicitly present, infer a concise business impact statement from the description, justification, priority, and overall context.\n  - Clearly explain negative business and operational consequences.\n  - Minimum 10 words, maximum 60 words.\n  - Do not omit this field.\n  - If absolutely no meaningful inference can be made, return an empty string.\n\nValidation and fallback:\n- After extraction, if Description or Name is empty but the text clearly contains a sentence starting with “I am requesting” or a line with a person’s name/title, use those as Description/Name respectively.\n- ProjectName is mandatory.\n- If Reason text is long, apply the mapping heuristics to that text.\n- Extract values against each attribute.\n- If a field value is missing, return an empty string for that field.\n\nMandatory completion rule:\n- Before returning the JSON, verify that every key in the schema is present exactly once.\n- \"ImpactIfNotImpl\" is mandatory.\n- If \"ImpactIfNotImpl\" was not directly extracted, generate it from the description, justification, reason, priority, and overall context.\n- Never leave out the \"ImpactIfNotImpl\" key.\n\nOutput:\n- Return exactly one JSON object.\n- Include all 10 keys exactly as defined in the schema.\n- Do not omit any key, even if empty.\n- UserIntent must be exactly one of: CREATE_CHANGE_REQUEST, HELP_ASSISTANCE.\n- Do not return markdown, explanation, or additional text.\n- Strictly return only valid JSON object.\n\nRequired JSON schema:\n{\n  \"Description\": \"\",\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Number\": \"\",\n  \"Reason\": \"\",\n  \"ProjectName\": \"\",\n  \"Priority\": \"\",\n  \"Justification\": \"\",\n  \"Comments\": \"\",\n  \"ImpactIfNotImpl\": \"\",\n  \"UserIntent\": \"\"\n}\n\nInput:\n1. Raw document text:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"Description\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Name\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Number\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Reason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ProjectName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Priority\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Justification\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Comments\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ImpactIfNotImpl\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"UserIntent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n                \"CREATE_CHANGE_REQUEST\",\n                \"HELP_ASSISTANCE\"\n            ]\n        }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n        \"Description\",\n        \"Name\",\n        \"Number\",\n        \"Reason\",\n        \"ProjectName\",\n        \"Priority\",\n        \"Justification\",\n        \"Comments\",\n        \"ImpactIfNotImpl\",\n        \"UserIntent\"\n    ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
