                  "code": "PRJ_PJE_LLM_STRATEGIC_GENERATE_PAYLOAD",
                  "id": "strategic_1774003261712",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "strategic_1774003261714_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an information extraction engine. You will receive noisy, table-like text  (Markdown/CSV-style with pipes, repeated columns, broken lines) or simple text and Json content only. Your task is to extract specific fields reliably. Follow the steps exactly and return only one JSON object.\n\nContext priority rules:\n- The latest user message is the highest priority source for corrections or overrides.\n- If the latest user message explicitly provides Project, Project Name, or ProjectName, use that value for ProjectName even when the attachment or prior history has a different value.\n- Use Strategic Agent chat history only to understand follow-up corrections and prior failure context; do not copy old invalid values when the latest user message corrects them.\n\nParsing and normalization steps (do all):\n1) Normalize:\n- Replace multiple spaces/newlines with single spaces where sentences were wrapped mid-line.\n- Remove table artifacts like leading/trailing pipes (|), header separators (---), duplicate columns, and repeated rows.\n- Keep meaningful punctuation.\n2) Canonicalize keys by matching common variants:\n- ProjectName: match any of [\"Organization\", \"Project\", \"Project Name\"].\n- Name: This is mandatory to be extracted. Read the given text content and extract/generate a meaningful Summary/Title from it.\n- Priority: match \"Priority\".\n- Description: Generate from the given complete text information or match [\"Change Description\", \"Description\"].\n- Reason: match [\"Change Reason\", \"Reason\"].\n- Justification: Generate from overall text info or match [\"Budget Impact\", \"Scope Impact\", \"Timeline Impact\", \"Justification\"] and concatenate in that order if multiple are present.\n- Comments: Generate a meaningful approval/review comment that summarizes the given context.\n- ImpactIfNotImpl : Based on the text context given, generate/extract a concise, professional, and business-focused \"Impact if Not Implemented\" comment suitable for entry in a project change management system.\n3) Duplication rule: If a value appears multiple times, choose the most complete and least truncated sentence.\n4) Cleaning rule: Remove trailing periods only if they are not part of a sentence. Preserve meaningful full sentences.\n\nField rules and defaults:\n- Description: Write a description of the change request. Include a brief summary of the issue and the impact of the change on project budget and timelines if any. Use a minimum of 10 words and a maximum of 30 words.\n- Reason: Map the found text to one of [ \"ORA_GENERAL\", \"ORA_DESIGN_CHANGE\", \"ORA_CLIENT_REQUEST\", \"ORA_TECHNICAL_ISSUE\" , \"ORA_OTHER\"]. Heuristics:\n  - If mentions “client”, “customer requested”, or “stakeholder requested” -> \"ORA_CLIENT_REQUEST\"\n  - If mentions “bug”, “error”, “defect”, “issue”, “technical limitation” -> \"ORA_TECHNICAL_ISSUE\"\n  - If mentions “design”, “spec change”, “UI/UX change” -> \"ORA_DESIGN_CHANGE\"\n  - If mentions “compliance”, “policy”, “security”, “governance” without other matches -> \"ORA_OTHER\"\n  - If you are not able to map to one of the given reasons, Then use -> \"ORA_GENERAL\"\n- ProjectName: Mandatory. Extract the project name using this priority order:\n  - First look for explicit labels: \"Project:\", \"Project Name:\", \"Organization:\", or \"ProjectName:\".\n  - Remove surrounding quotes, brackets, parentheses, and trailing punctuation.\n  - If multiple project names appear, choose the one from the subject line first; otherwise choose the most specific and complete project name.\n  - If no explicit label exists, look for phrases ending with \"project\", such as \"North Ridge Substation Upgrade project\", and extract the project name without the word \"project\" unless it is part of the official name.\n  - If no project name can be found, return an empty string.\n- Name: Change request title/name. If not explicitly found, extract/generate a meaningful change request title from the subject or overall context, max 80 characters.\n- Number: Get change request number information in the given text input OR Generate from extracted name information . If the value is still null or blank generate a meaningful value from Name.\n- Priority: One of [\"HIGH\",\"MEDIUM\",\"LOW\"]; if unclear -> \"MEDIUM\".\n- Justification: Based on the Reason Extracted, Change Description, explain why the change request is necessary. Use a minimum of 10 words and a maximum of 60 words.\n  - Mention the business justification\n- Comments: The comment should be short not more than 150 character:\n  - Summarize the requested change\n  - Use formal, professional language\n  - Be written as a single well-structured comment paragraph\n- ImpactIfNotImpl : Based on given text information generate what will happen if this request is not implemented make this short. Use a minimum of 10 words and a maximum of 60 words.\n  - Match any of [\"Impact if Not Implemented\", \"Impact If Not Implemented\", \"Impact if not implemented\", \"Business Impact if Not Implemented\", \"Risk if Not Implemented\"].\n  - If the source text explicitly contains an impact-if-not-implemented statement, extract it.\n  - If it is not explicitly present, infer a concise business impact statement from the description, justification, priority, and overall context.\n  - Clearly explain the negative business and operational consequences\n  - Do not omit this field.\n  - If absolutely no meaningful inference can be made, return an empty string.\n  - Note the risk if the change is not implemented\n\nValidation and fallback:\n- After extraction, if Description or Name is empty but the text clearly contains a sentence starting with “I am requesting” or a line with a person’s name/title, use those as Description/Name respectively.\n- ProjectName field is mandatory.\n- If Reason text is long, apply the mapping heuristics to that text.\n- Extract Value against each attribute.\n- Name : Filed is Mandatory to generate and generate a meaningful change request name form the given subject from text limiting to 80 character.\n- Number : field is mandatory if not found generate a meaningful number form the given Subject and do not include space as character make this short not more than 50 character.\n\nMandatory completion rule:\n- Before returning the JSON, verify that every key in the schema is present exactly once.\n- \"ImpactIfNotImpl\" is mandatory.\n- If \"ImpactIfNotImpl\" was not directly extracted, you must generate it from the description, justification, reason, priority, and overall change context.\n- Never leave out the \"ImpactIfNotImpl\" key.\n- If no direct or inferred value is possible, return \"ImpactIfNotImpl\": \"\".\n\nOutput:\n- Return exactly one JSON object.\n- Include all 9 keys exactly as defined in the schema.\n- Do not omit any key, even if empty.\n- Do not return markdown, explanation, or additional text.\n- Strictly return only valid JSON object.\n- If a field value is missing, return an empty string for that field.\n- Strictly return below required JSON schema:\n{\n  \"Description\": \"\",\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Number\": \"\",\n  \"Reason\": \"\",\n  \"ProjectName\": \"\",\n  \"Priority\": \"\",\n  \"Justification\": \"\",\n  \"Comments\": \"\",\n  \"ImpactIfNotImpl\": \"\"\n}\n\nInput:\n1. Raw document text:\n 1.1 {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJE_LOOP_STRATEGIC_EACH_FILE.$currentItem.content}}\n 1.2 {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n2. Strategic Agent chat history and retained context for follow-up corrections:\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjeVarConvStrategicAgentChatHistory}}\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjeVarConvActiveAtomicAgentDetails}}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"Description\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"Name\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"Number\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"Reason\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"ProjectName\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"Priority\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"Justification\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"Comments\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"ImpactIfNotImpl\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"Description\",\n    \"Name\",\n    \"Number\",\n    \"Reason\",\n    \"ProjectName\",\n    \"Priority\",\n    \"Justification\",\n    \"Comments\",\n    \"ImpactIfNotImpl\"\n  ]\n}",
